<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-review-normal> {
  ex:rv-growth-chart rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "More draws from one assumed stable normal method"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:binEdges ex:nn-ge0 ;
    cd:body "The histograms use successive prefixes of one simulated Normal sequence with expectation 10.00 mg/L and SD 0.10 mg/L. Bin edges and the generating model remain fixed."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:Histogram ;
    cd:hasHistogramState ex:rv-growth-state1000 ;
    cd:hasHistogramState ex:rv-growth-state100 ;
    cd:hasHistogramState ex:rv-growth-state20 ;
    cd:hasHistogramState ex:rv-growth-state50 ;
    cd:histogramNormalization "density" ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:rv-growth20 ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Individual nitrate result"@en ;
    cd:xAxisUnit "mg/L" ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Simulated density"@en ;
    cd:yAxisUnit "L/mg" .
  ex:rv-growth-code dct:hasPart ex:rv-growth-functions ;
    rdf:type cd:CodeExample ;
    skos:prefLabel "Replay each published normal-simulation prefix"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:code """# Assumed normal generator, not fitted or measured validation data.
M <- 20 # Try 20, 50, 100, 1000. The browser uses these saved prefixes.
stopifnot(M %in% c(20,50,100,1000))
state <- 20261102; x <- numeric(M)
for(i in seq_len(M)) {
  state <- (16807 * state) %% 2147483647
  x[i] <- 10 + .10 * qnorm(state/2147483647)
}
edges <- seq(9.60,10.40,by=.05)
h <- hist(x,breaks=edges,right=FALSE,plot=FALSE)
cat('M:',M,'counted:',sum(h$counts),'\\n')
cat('Counts:',h$counts,'\\n')
plot(h,freq=FALSE,col='#8ecae6',xlab='Nitrate result (mg/L)',
     ylab='Simulated density (L/mg)',main='Assumed stable normal generator')
""" ;
    cd:editable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:executable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:programmingLanguage "r" ;
    cd:showsResource ex:normal-measurement-model .
  ex:rv-growth-functions rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-growth-functions-entry .
  ex:rv-growth-functions-entry rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "R functions and the deterministic stream"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **Choose the sample size.** `c` lists the allowed result counts. `%in%` checks whether `M` belongs to that list, and `stopifnot` enforces this choice.
- **Prepare the simulation.** `numeric` allocates the result vector; `seq_len` supplies the iteration indices.
- **Generate reproducible results.** The Park–Miller recurrence updates an integer-valued state using multiplication and the remainder operator `%%`. `qnorm` transforms the resulting uniform fractions into standard-normal values. Scaling and shifting set the stated SD and mean.
- **Build the histogram.** `seq` creates fixed bin edges. `hist` computes and draws density bins whose left edges belong to the bin.
- **Check the counts.** `sum` totals the bin counts; `cat` reports that total alongside `M` so that count conservation can be checked."""@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:rv-growth-state100 rdf:type cd:HistogramState ;
    skos:prefLabel "100 results"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The first 100 results from the same simulated sequence."@en ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:rv-growth100 .
  ex:rv-growth-state1000 rdf:type cd:HistogramState ;
    skos:prefLabel "1,000 results"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The first 1,000 results from the same simulated sequence."@en ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:nn-growth-data .
  ex:rv-growth-state20 rdf:type cd:HistogramState ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 results"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The first 20 results from the same simulated sequence."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:rv-growth20 .
  ex:rv-growth-state50 rdf:type cd:HistogramState ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 results"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The first 50 results from the same simulated sequence."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:rv-growth50 .
  ex:rv-n07-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "One unchanged sample can produce different results"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:rv-n08-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "More results reveal the assumed distribution more clearly"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
}

