<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-review-p1-scenes> {
  ex:p1-censor rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Censoring: respect the reporting limit"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- ==A non-detect locates the result below a reporting threshold.==
- **Replacing all low results by one value:** creates an artificial pile-up.
- **Model explicitly:** observation process and reporting threshold."""@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-mix rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mixtures: define the population"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **Multiple sources:** pooling can create skewness or several peaks.
- ==Assess the model for the defined sampling population.==
- **Before fitting:** identify the sampling population."""@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-population-cards rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-censor ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-mix ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-sites .
  ex:p1-route rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-route1 ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-route2 ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-route3 ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-route4 ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-route5 ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:p1-route6 .
  ex:p1-route1 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Why do measurements vary?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Observe repeated results and define the random quantity."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-route2 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Why a bell-shaped model?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Combine suitable independent additive effects."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-route3 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Why a long right tail?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Model relative effects on the log scale."@en ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-route4 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "How random is estimated spread?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Study sample variances and standardized means."@en ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-route5 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "How can we compare methods?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Describe variance ratios with the F distribution."@en ;
    cd:position "5"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-route6 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "How do we check our models?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Compare data with model quantiles, CDFs and expected counts."@en ;
    cd:position "6"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:p1-series-A rdf:type cd:ChartGroup ;
    skos:prefLabel "A: sample SD 0.056"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:p1-data-A .
  ex:p1-series-B rdf:type cd:ChartGroup ;
    skos:prefLabel "B: sample SD 0.086"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:p1-data-B .
  ex:p1-series-C rdf:type cd:ChartGroup ;
    skos:prefLabel "C: sample SD 0.128"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:p1-data-C .
  ex:p1-series-chart rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "Three illustrative series, one common concentration axis"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Six results per constructed teaching series, all with mean 10.000 mg/L. Sample variances A 0.00316, B 0.00748, C 0.01648 (mg/L) squared; corresponding sample SDs about 0.056, 0.086 and 0.128 mg/L. Their variance markers appear in the repeated-sampling simulation."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:DotPlot ;
    cd:hasChartGroup ex:p1-series-A ;
    cd:hasChartGroup ex:p1-series-B ;
    cd:hasChartGroup ex:p1-series-C ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Complete illustrative series"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Nitrate result"@en ;
    cd:yAxisUnit "mg/L" .
  ex:p1-sites rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sites: environmental variation"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **Different sites:** genuine environmental variation and possible spatial dependence.
- ==Define the population of sites and sampling conditions.==
- **Reporting target:** arithmetic expectation and a typical log-scale center answer different questions."""@en ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-review-pdf-cdf> {
  ex:pc-area dct:hasPart ex:pc-area-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:formulaLabel "Probability is model density integrated over an interval"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:pc-area-symbol ;
    cd:latex "P(a\\le X\\le b)=\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx=F(b)-F(a)" .
  ex:pc-area-entry dct:references ex:pc-area-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Result, interval, integral and units"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-area-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:pc-area-entry .
  ex:pc-area-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **X**: Random individual nitrate concentration (mg/L).
- **x**: Concrete concentration coordinate (mg/L).
- **a, b**: Ordered lower and upper interval bounds (mg/L).
- **P**: Probability of the stated event (dimensionless).
- **f(x)**: Model probability density at x (L/mg).
- **F(x)**: Cumulative probability at or below x (dimensionless).
- **∫, dx**: Accumulate density over the interval; dx is an infinitesimal concentration increment (mg/L).
- **≤**: Includes the interval endpoints, each with zero point probability.
- **=, −**: Equality between equivalent probabilities; subtraction of the lower CDF value from the upper.

The density is nonnegative and has total area one. Integrating density times concentration gives a dimensionless probability."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "P,a,b,X,\\le,\\int,f(x),dx,F,=,-" ;
    cd:symbol "interval probability and density area" .
  ex:pc-below rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "How much is below a limit?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The cumulative distribution gives the probability at or below a threshold."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-density rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "Finite histogram versus an assumed population density"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The histogram summarizes the simulated nitrate sample; the smooth curve is the selected model density. The shaded interval uses the selected bounds, so its area can be compared with the observed sample fraction."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ;
    cd:experimentKind "distribution" ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-Mreference ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-seed-reference ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-family ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-location ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-probability-fixed ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-scale ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-threshold0 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-view0 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-width ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Nitrate result (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Empirical and model density"@en .
  ex:pc-density-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "Area under the density gives interval probability"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:pc-family rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Model: 0 smooth bell, 1 bounded flat"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "0.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "family" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "0.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "6"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-functions dct:hasPart ex:pc-functions-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:formulaLabel "Accumulate · read the local slope · reverse the question"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:pc-functions-symbol ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:pc-quantile-symbol ;
    cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}F(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{x}f(t)\\,dt\\\\f(x)=F'(x)\\quad\\text{where the derivative exists}\\\\x_p=F^{-1}(p)\\end{gathered}" .
  ex:pc-functions-entry dct:references ex:pc-functions-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Accumulation and local slope"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-functions-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:pc-functions-entry ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:pc-quantile-entry .
  ex:pc-functions-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **X**: Random concentration (mg/L).
- **x**: Concrete concentration threshold (mg/L).
- **F(x)**: Cumulative probability at or below x (dimensionless).
- **P, ≤**: Probability of an event; at or below the threshold.
- **f(t)**: Probability density at concentration t (L/mg).
- **t, dt**: Integration coordinate and its infinitesimal increment (mg/L).
- **∫, −∞**: Integrate up to x over an unbounded lower range.
- **F′(x)**: Derivative of F with respect to x; the local slope (L/mg).
- **=**: Equality linking the expressions.

Conditions: the integral representation uses an absolutely continuous model. The slope equals f where the derivative relation holds. Every distribution has a CDF; existence of a PDF requires additional conditions."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "F(x),P,X,\\le,\\int,-\\infty,f(t),dt,F',=" ;
    cd:presentationDefinition """- X: random concentration; x: threshold; t: integration coordinate (mg/L).
- f: density (L/mg); F and P: unitless probabilities at or below x.
- Integral: accumulate from unbounded lower limit to x; dt: concentration increment.
- For an absolutely continuous model, prime means derivative with respect to x; equals links the expressions. The density relation applies where the CDF has the stated derivative."""@en ;
    cd:symbol "general PDF and CDF" .
  ex:pc-growth-info rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "A larger simulated sample reveals the generating distribution more clearly while the method's population spread stays unchanged."@en .
  ex:pc-inverse rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Which limit gives a chosen probability?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Choose a cumulative probability. The quantile gives its corresponding threshold."@en ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-linked rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "One shared threshold links area and accumulation"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The density and CDF panels share the selected concentration threshold. The shaded density area and the marked CDF height represent the same accumulated probability."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ;
    cd:experimentKind "distribution" ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-Mreference ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-seed-reference ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-family ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-location ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-probability ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-scale ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-threshold ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-view1 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:pc-width-fixed ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Shared threshold (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Probability density and cumulative probability"@en .
  ex:pc-linked-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "A quantile turns probability into a threshold"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:pc-location rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Assumed model expectation (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "location" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-phi-chart rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "The standard-normal density is one particular PDF"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The standard-Normal density is symmetric about zero and reaches its maximum there. The horizontal coordinate is standardized distance; the vertical coordinate is density per standardized unit."@en ;
    cd:chartPresentation "complete" ;
    cd:chartType cd:LineChart ;
    cd:chartYMaximum "0.42"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:chartYMinimum "0.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:showChartPoints "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:usesDataset ex:l5-c14-standard-normal ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Standardized coordinate z"@en ;
    cd:xAxisUnit "1" ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Standard-normal density φ"@en ;
    cd:yAxisUnit "per z-unit" .
  ex:pc-probability rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Chosen cumulative probability p"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "0.95"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "probability" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "0.99"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "5"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-probability-fixed rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quantile question reserved for the next scene"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "0.95"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "probability" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "0.95"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "0.95"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "0.01"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "5"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-process-info rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "A measurement model connects the reported result with the contributions of injection, flow, temperature and electronics. Repetition under the same conditions reveals their combined variation."@en .
  ex:pc-quantile-entry dct:references ex:pc-quantile-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cumulative probability to concentration"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-quantile-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **p**: Chosen cumulative probability, strictly between zero and one.
- **$x_p$**: Concentration quantile at probability $p$ (mg/L); subscript $p$ identifies the probability.
- **F⁻¹(p)**: Quantile function, the generalized inverse CDF evaluated at p.

The generalized inverse is the greatest lower bound of thresholds whose cumulative probability is at least $p$. For continuous, strictly increasing $F$, it is the usual inverse function. In these continuous examples, $p = 0.95$ places 95% probability at or below $x_p$."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "x_p,F^{-1},p" ;
    cd:presentationDefinition """- p: chosen probability strictly between zero and one.
- Subscript p labels concentration quantile x p (mg/L).
- F inverse: quantile function; the usual inverse for continuous strictly increasing F.
- In these continuous models, p=0.95 means 95% at or below the limit."""@en ;
    cd:symbol "quantile as the reversed cumulative question" .
  ex:pc-questions rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:pc-below ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:pc-inverse ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:pc-range .
  ex:pc-questions-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "Which questions can a probability distribution answer?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:pc-range rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "How often in a range?"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Choose a concentration interval. Its probability is the area under the model density."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:pc-scale rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
