<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-review-v3> {
  ex:v3-eta dct:hasPart ex:v3-eta-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:formulaLabel "Random standardized variable Z, observed standardized value z"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:v3-eta-symbol ;
    cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}X\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mu,\\sigma^2),\\quad Z=\\frac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\sim\\mathcal N(0,1)\\\\z=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}=\\frac{10.20-10.00}{0.10}=2\\end{gathered}" .
  ex:v3-eta-entry dct:references ex:v3-eta-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Result, expectation and known SD"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:v3-eta-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:v3-eta-entry .
  ex:v3-eta-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **X**: Random nitrate concentration (mg/L).
- **x**: Concrete result, 10.20 mg/L.
- **μ**: Known model expectation, 10.00 mg/L.
- **σ**: Known positive model SD, 0.10 mg/L.
- **σ²**: Model variance ((mg/L)²).
- **Z**: Standardized random variable, with mean zero and variance one under the Normal model.
- **z**: Concrete standardized distance, 2 here (dimensionless).
- **N, ∼**: Normal distribution, parameterized by mean and variance; follows that distribution.
- **−, /, ², =**: Subtraction, division, squaring and equality defining or evaluating a value.

Subtracting μ and dividing by σ cancels concentration units. Standardization preserves distributional shape; a standard-normal reference requires a Normal starting model."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "X,Z,z,x,\\mu,\\sigma,\\mathcal N,\\sim,{}^2,=,-,/" ;
    cd:symbol "standardized result" .
  ex:v3-normal-coordinate rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "First locate the result in known SD units"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The marker places the selected nitrate result on the Normal density with expectation 10.00 mg/L and known SD 0.10 mg/L. Its standardized distance is shown alongside the plot."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ;
    cd:experimentKind "normal" ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-alpha01 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-inverse ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-mu ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-sigma ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-threshold ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:v3-view5 ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Concentration (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Normal density"@en .
  ex:v3-pearson-entry dct:references ex:v3-pearson-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Five fixed categories, four count directions"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:v3-pearson-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:v3-pearson-entry .
  ex:v3-pearson-sum dct:hasPart ex:v3-pearson-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:formulaLabel "Square each count discrepancy, weight it, then add"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:v3-pearson-symbol ;
    cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}q=\\sum_{j=1}^{5}\\frac{(O_j-E_j)^2}{E_j}\\\\\\frac{(4-10)^2}{10}=3.6\\\\q=3.6+3.2+0.4+0.8+3.6=11.6\\end{gathered}" .
  ex:v3-pearson-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **q**: Observed Pearson statistic (dimensionless).
- **j**: Index of the five fixed diameter categories.
- **Oⱼ**: Observed particle count in category j.
- **Eⱼ**: Positive expected count in category j under the fixed model.
- **Σ, +**: Sum all category contributions.
- **−, ², /**: Subtract expected from observed count, square, then divide by expected count.
- **=**: Equality giving the calculation.

In the first category O = 4 and E = 10. A fixed total of 100 and fixed category probabilities leave four degrees of freedom. The chi-square reference is approximate and requires independent classifications, exhaustive prespecified categories and adequate expected counts."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "q,\\sum,j,O_j,E_j,=,-,+,/,{}^2" ;
    cd:symbol "Pearson weighted count discrepancies" .
  ex:v3-view5 rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Coordinate-only teaching view"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "view" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "5.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "20"^^xsd:integer .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-student-t> {
  ex:l5-student-t rdf:type cd:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Student-t inference under iid normal sampling"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinition ex:l5-t16-definition .
  ex:l5-t16-definition rdf:type cd:Definition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "For independent identically distributed normal observations with positive population variance, the sample mean standardized by its estimated standard error has a Student-t distribution with sample size minus one degrees of freedom. The sample mean and sample variance are independent under this model. Replacing known population SD by random sample SD changes the reference distribution. Exact small-sample t inference requires the normal sampling assumptions; a small estimated SE does not establish them."@en .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-tf-distributions-only> {
  ex:dist-devices-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-devices-title .
  ex:dist-devices-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "A variance comparison needs two independent groups"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:dist-f rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "Independent variance estimates form a random ratio"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The histogram contains variance ratios from independent Normal sample pairs with equal true variances. The F curve uses numerator and denominator degrees of freedom in the displayed group order."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ;
    cd:experimentKind "f-ratio" ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:dist-f-view ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-M ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-nA ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-nB ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-reverse ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-seed ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-sigma ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Ratio of independent sample variances"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en .
  ex:dist-f-collect rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Collect, repeat, plot"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "One ratio per independent sample pair. Equal true variances cancel."@en ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-f-draw rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Draw two independent samples"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Six normally distributed measurement results per group. Population means may differ."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-f-edge1 rdf:type cd:DiagramEdge ;
    skos:prefLabel "estimate"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:sourceNode ex:dist-f-draw ;
    cd:targetNode ex:dist-f-estimate .
  ex:dist-f-edge2 rdf:type cd:DiagramEdge ;
    skos:prefLabel "normalize"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:sourceNode ex:dist-f-estimate ;
    cd:targetNode ex:dist-f-normalize .
  ex:dist-f-edge3 rdf:type cd:DiagramEdge ;
    skos:prefLabel "one ratio"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:sourceNode ex:dist-f-normalize ;
    cd:targetNode ex:dist-f-collect .
  ex:dist-f-estimate rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Estimate both variances"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Use each sample's own estimated mean."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-f-intro-entry dct:references ex:dist-f-intro-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Two independent estimates; numerator B, denominator A"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-f-intro-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-intro-formula .
  ex:dist-f-intro-flow rdf:type cd:FlowDiagram ;
    skos:prefLabel "Repeat two independent variance-estimation experiments"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Each independent pair of complete samples produces two variance estimates and one normalized ratio. Repeating the pair reveals the ratio's sampling distribution."@en ;
    cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-f-edge1 ;
    cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-f-edge2 ;
    cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-f-edge3 ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-f-collect ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-f-draw ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-f-estimate ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-f-normalize .
  ex:dist-f-intro-formula dct:hasPart ex:dist-f-intro-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:formulaLabel "The ordered ratio of two normalized variance estimates"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:dist-f-intro-symbol ;
    cd:latex "F=\\frac{S_B^2/\\sigma_B^2}{S_A^2/\\sigma_A^2}" .
  ex:dist-f-intro-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-intro-title .
  ex:dist-f-intro-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:dist-f-intro-entry .
  ex:dist-f-intro-scene dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-f-intro-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-f-intro-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-f-intro-v ;
    cd:narration "Each independent pair of Normal samples supplies two sample variances. Scale each estimate by its own true variance, then take the ordered B/A ratio. Repeating this experiment produces an F distribution. With equal true variances, the scaling cancels and the ratio uses the sample variances directly."@en .
  ex:dist-f-intro-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **F**: Random normalized variance ratio (dimensionless).
- **A, B**: Independent groups; B is the numerator and A the denominator.
- **$S_B^2, S_A^2$**: Random sample variances about each group's estimated mean ($\\mathrm{(mg/L)^2}$).
- **$σ_B^2, σ_A^2$**: Corresponding fixed positive population variances ($\\mathrm{(mg/L)^2}$).
- **²**: Square an SD to obtain variance.
- **/**: Inner divisions normalize each sample variance; the outer fraction forms B/A.
- **=**: Equality defining F.

Conditions: measurements are independent and identically Normal within each group, and the groups are independent. Group means may differ. Each variance uses divisor sample count minus one; six measurements per group give five degrees of freedom each. Equal true variances cancel, leaving the sample-variance ratio."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "F,S_B^2,\\sigma_B^2,S_A^2,\\sigma_A^2" ;
    cd:symbol "normalized variance ratio" .
  ex:dist-f-intro-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "Independent normalized variance estimates form an F ratio"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:dist-f-intro-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DiagramRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-intro-flow .
  ex:dist-f-normalize rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Normalize and divide"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Normalize each estimate by its true variance; take B over A."@en ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-f-view rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Distribution construction and ordered degrees of freedom"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "view" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "3.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "20"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "A random estimated denominator creates heavier tails"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Each histogram entry comes from one complete Normal sample with true SD 0.10 mg/L."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ;
    cd:experimentKind "student" ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:dist-t-n2 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:dist-t-view ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-M ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-seed ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-sigma ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Studentized mean departure"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en .
  ex:dist-t-collect rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Collect, repeat, plot"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "One standardized value per complete sample. What distribution appears?"@en ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t-compare rdf:type cd:ChartDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "More degrees of freedom approach the normal density"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The two Student densities use the selected sample sizes, each with sample count minus one degrees of freedom. The standard-Normal curve provides their common reference on the same standardized axis."@en ;
    cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ;
    cd:experimentKind "student" ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:dist-t-view ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-Mreference ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-comp30 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-n4 ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-seed-reference ;
    cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-sigma ;
    cd:xAxisLabel "Student variable"@en ;
    cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en .
  ex:dist-t-draw rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Take six measurements"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Independent normally distributed results from one fixed population."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t-edge1 rdf:type cd:DiagramEdge ;
    skos:prefLabel "estimate"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:sourceNode ex:dist-t-draw ;
    cd:targetNode ex:dist-t-estimate .
  ex:dist-t-edge2 rdf:type cd:DiagramEdge ;
    skos:prefLabel "center and scale"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:sourceNode ex:dist-t-estimate ;
    cd:targetNode ex:dist-t-standardize .
  ex:dist-t-edge3 rdf:type cd:DiagramEdge ;
    skos:prefLabel "one value"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:sourceNode ex:dist-t-standardize ;
    cd:targetNode ex:dist-t-collect .
  ex:dist-t-estimate rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Estimate mean and SD"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Both estimates change from sample to sample."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t-intro-entry dct:references ex:dist-t-intro-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "A random numerator and a random denominator"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t-intro-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-intro-formula .
  ex:dist-t-intro-flow rdf:type cd:FlowDiagram ;
    skos:prefLabel "Repeat the complete mean-and-SD experiment"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "The population stays fixed. Each new sample produces a new mean, a new estimated standard error and one standardized value."@en ;
    cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-t-edge1 ;
    cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-t-edge2 ;
    cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-t-edge3 ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-t-collect ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-t-draw ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-t-estimate ;
    cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-t-standardize .
  ex:dist-t-intro-formula dct:hasPart ex:dist-t-intro-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:formulaLabel "A mean standardized with its estimated standard error"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:dist-t-intro-symbol ;
    cd:latex "T=\\frac{\\bar X-\\mu}{S/\\sqrt n},\\qquad n=6" .
  ex:dist-t-intro-h rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-intro-title .
  ex:dist-t-intro-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:dist-t-intro-entry .
  ex:dist-t-intro-scene dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-t-intro-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-t-intro-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-t-intro-v ;
    cd:narration "Repeated six-measurement experiments produce different sample means and SDs. Subtract the true mean from each estimated mean and divide by its estimated standard error. Under independent Normal sampling, these standardized values follow a Student distribution with five degrees of freedom."@en .
  ex:dist-t-intro-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **T**: Random standardized sample mean (dimensionless).
- **X̄**: Random sample mean (mg/L); the bar denotes averaging.
- **μ**: Fixed true population mean (mg/L).
- **S**: Positive random sample SD estimated from the same sample (mg/L).
- **n**: Dimensionless sample count, six here.
- **S / √n**: Estimated standard error of the mean (mg/L); the square root is positive.
- **−, /, =**: Centre the mean, divide by its estimated standard error, and define T.
- **Comma**: Separates the definition from the stated sample count.

Condition: independent, identically distributed Normal measurement results. Sample variance uses divisor n − 1. Across complete samples, both estimated mean and SD vary while the population stays fixed."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "T,\\bar X,\\mu,S,n" ;
    cd:symbol "standardized sample mean" .
  ex:dist-t-intro-title rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    skos:prefLabel "Estimating the standard error changes the reference to t"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean .
  ex:dist-t-intro-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DiagramRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-intro-flow .
  ex:dist-t-n2 rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Measurements per complete series"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "n" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "200.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "2.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t-standardize rdf:type cd:DiagramNode ;
    skos:prefLabel "Standardize the mean"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Center at the true mean; divide by the estimated standard error."@en ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:dist-t-view rdf:type cd:ExperimentParameter ;
    skos:prefLabel "Distribution construction and shape"@en ;
    cd:adjustableParameter "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:numericValue "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterKey "view" ;
    cd:parameterMaximum "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterMinimum "4.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:parameterStep "1.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cd:position "20"^^xsd:integer .
}

