  ex:tf-b1 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "9.55"@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-b2 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "9.85"@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-b3 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.00"@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-b4 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.00"@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-b5 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.15"@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-b6 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.45"@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-col-a rdf:type cd:TableColumn ;
    skos:prefLabel "Device A (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-col-b rdf:type cd:TableColumn ;
    skos:prefLabel "Device B (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-col-pa rdf:type cd:TableColumn ;
    skos:prefLabel "Same device A (mg/L)"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-data rdf:type cd:TableDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "Fictional CRM results in mg/L: device A is retained unchanged"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableColumn ex:tf-col-a ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-row1 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-row2 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-row3 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-row4 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-row5 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-row6 .
  ex:tf-denom1 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Small denominator, large statistic"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- Small estimated SE can magnify either sign of mean departure.
- True generating SD stays fixed."""@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-denom2 rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Heavier tails from an estimated standard error"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- Symmetric t density: lower peak, heavier tails than normal.
- Each complete sample contributes one studentized mean.
- Normal sampling makes mean and variance independent."""@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-denominator rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:tf-denom1 ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:tf-denom2 .
  ex:tf-f-law dct:hasPart ex:tf-f-law-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Under equal population variances the unknown common variance cancels, leaving the random sample-variance ratio B/A. Each group is iid normal and the groups are independent. Equal group means are not required."@en ;
    cd:formulaLabel "Two independent scaled variances"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:tf-f-law-symbol ;
    cd:latex "Q_j=\\frac{\\nu_j S_j^2}{\\sigma_j^2}\\sim\\chi^2_{\\nu_j},\\qquad F=\\frac{Q_B/\\nu_B}{Q_A/\\nu_A}\\sim F_{\\nu_B,\\nu_A}" .
  ex:tf-f-law-entry dct:references ex:tf-f-law-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ordered df and independence"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-f-law-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:tf-f-law-entry .
  ex:tf-f-law-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **$j$**: Group index $A$ or $B$.
- **$ν_j$**: Group $j$'s sample count minus one, giving its degrees of freedom.
- **$S_j^2$**: Random sample variance about group $j$'s fitted mean ($\\mathrm{(mg/L)^2}$).
- **$σ_j^2$**: Positive true variance of group $j$ ($\\mathrm{(mg/L)^2}$).
- **$Q_j$**: Scaled sample variance, $\\frac{ν_j S_j^2}{σ_j^2}$ (dimensionless).
- **$F$**: Resulting dimensionless random ratio; also the name of its reference distribution.
- **$()^2, /, =, ∼$**: Variance from squaring an SD; division; equality; follows the named distribution.
- **Comma**: Orders distribution parameters: numerator B degrees of freedom, then denominator A.

The Normal samples and groups are independent, making $Q_A$ and $Q_B$ independent chi-square variables. Both degrees of freedom are five here. Equal true variances cancel; otherwise normalize the sample-variance ratio by the true $B/A$ variance ratio."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "j,Q_j,\\nu_j,S_j^2,\\sigma_j^2,F" ;
    cd:symbol "F construction" .
  ex:tf-pa1 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "9.95"@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pa2 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.05"@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pa3 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.10"@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pa4 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.10"@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pa5 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.15"@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pa6 rdf:type cd:TableCell ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "10.25"@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pair-data dct:references ex:tf-data ;
    rdf:type cd:TableDefinition ;
    skos:prefLabel "Independent groups; concentrations in mg/L"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableColumn ex:tf-col-b ;
    cd:hasTableColumn ex:tf-col-pa ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-pair1 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-pair2 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-pair3 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-pair4 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-pair5 ;
    cd:hasTableRow ex:tf-pair6 .
  ex:tf-pair1 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-b1 ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-pa1 ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pair2 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-b2 ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-pa2 ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pair3 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-b3 ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-pa3 ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pair4 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-b4 ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-pa4 ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pair5 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-b5 ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-pa5 ;
    cd:position "5"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-pair6 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-b6 ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-pa6 ;
    cd:position "6"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-ratio dct:hasPart ex:tf-ratio-legend ;
    rdf:type cd:MathExpression ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "A retains mean 10.10 and SD 0.10 mg/L. B has mean 10.00 and SD 0.30 mg/L. B's observed mean is closer to the CRM, while A's observed spread is smaller. Trueness and precision are different properties; six results do not establish either population property."@en ;
    cd:formulaLabel "The observed sample-variance ratio is nine"@en ;
    cd:hasSymbol ex:tf-ratio-symbol ;
    cd:latex "f=\\frac{s_B^2}{s_A^2}=\\frac{0.090}{0.010}=9" .
  ex:tf-ratio-entry dct:references ex:tf-ratio-symbol ;
    rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Preserve B over A"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-ratio-legend rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:tf-ratio-entry .
  ex:tf-ratio-symbol rdf:type cd:MathSymbol ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **f**: Observed sample-variance ratio (dimensionless).
- **$s_B^2$**: Observed variance in group B, $0.090\\,\\mathrm{(mg/L)^2}$.
- **$s_A^2$**: Observed variance in group A, $0.010\\,\\mathrm{(mg/L)^2}$.
- **B, A**: Group subscripts specifying the prespecified numerator and denominator.
- **², /, =**: Squaring an SD to obtain variance, division and equality.

Each group contains six independent results, with independent groups. Each variance uses that group's fitted mean and divisor five. Concentration units cancel in B/A; the group order is fixed before inspecting the data."""@en ;
    cd:mathNotation "f,s_B^2,s_A^2" ;
    cd:symbol "observed variance ratio" .
  ex:tf-row1 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-a1 ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-row2 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-a2 ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-row3 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-a3 ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-row4 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasTableCell ex:tf-a4 ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:tf-row5 rdf:type cd:TableRow ;
